built binary confirm the check fires on an unlisted archived path under relative AND absolute file strings and on a non-plan artifact while keeping the root, admits listed paths under relative, absolute and backslash forms, and stays clean on clean comments, element-text hyphens and CDATA that resembles a comment. Disclosures. (1) SELF-COLLISION IN THE APPROVED PLAN, and the authority approved it: D8 required four distinct fail signatures on T-001, and FIX_DISTINCT_SIGNATURE_BUDGET is exactly 4, so the fourth planned red tripped the flailing detector and paused the task (event 6 escalation listing all four planned signatures). The executor resumed with a Reason citing D8 (event 7) and then landed production. The reds are genuine and the pairs audit is clean, but a plan whose red-first decomposition needs four distinct signatures in one task cannot be executed without an escalation-resume. The budget cannot distinguish a planned red-first sequence from an executor thrashing. Recorded as a finding; the repair is to cap planned reds per task at three or to teach the plan skill to split. (2) F54: exact project-relative identity is impossible at the emission site because parseGraceXmlArtifact never learns the project root, so the allowlist matches as a normalized suffix. Probed live: a same-named archived plan under a foreign project tree is silently admitted. Disclosed in the plan DESIGN, not hidden; exactness is a re-spec threading a root through roughly eighty call sites. (3) The new diagnostic names the file but not where in it, although the scanner holds the offset and NgraceIssue has an optional line field that the sibling xml.parse populates. Measured before judging: only about four emission sites in the product populate line, so the omission follows house behaviour and no criterion asked for a position. Recorded with a home rather than repaired at close, because repairing it needs a criterion that does not exist and authoring one post-hoc to bless code about to be written is the F28 shape. (4) F55: assertion.command-not-evaluated prints four byte-identical messages for four different commands - F40's class on a code this spec explicitly excludes. Recorded, not folded in. (5) The executor reported the ngrace-execute skill as stale on the fix budget. It is not; both canonical and packaged say two same-signature fails or four distinct signatures, which matches the binary. Correcting the record. (6) The authority's own execute prompt wrongly demanded assertion.change-not-approved from bare lint; default mode evaluates approved baselines only. Caught by the executor. (7) Teaching bytes were adjusted to match the already-written tests rather than the tests loosened to match production - the correct direction, preserving red-first.</Verdict></Verdicts><Decisions><Decision gate="apply" decision="permit"><Requirement id="plan-present" required="true" present="true" blocking="false">status=approved</Requirement><Requirement id="review-verdict" required="true" present="true" blocking="false">outcome=pass</Requirement><Requirement id="no-unresolved-satisfied-ac-clarification" required="true" present="true" blocking="false" /></Decision><Decision gate="archive" decision="permit"><Requirement id="no-open-epoch" required="true" present="true" blocking="false">run/ empty</Requirement></Decision></Decisions></C-ARTIFACT-VALIDITY></NgraceRunLedger>
